---
import CoachLayout from '../../layouts/CoachLayout.astro';
import { coach, exercises, practiceUrl } from '../../data/communication-coach';
import CoachPracticeLinks from '../../components/CoachPracticeLinks.astro';
---
<CoachLayout title="Communication Coach" path={coach.path} description="Five guided exercises to practise clear explanations, listening, reading comprehension, clarification, and constructive disagreement in ChatGPT or Claude.">
  <p>Created by <a href="/about">GG Nagarkar</a> for working professionals at any career stage. Practise for five or ten minutes, get specific feedback, and try again.</p>
  <p>Many people already communicate very well; others benefit from focused practice. This is a supportive space to practise, not a judgment of anyone’s ability or worth. As AI agents take on more work, clear explanations and careful understanding matter at every career stage.</p>
  <section aria-labelledby="start-heading">
    <h2 id="start-heading">Start practising</h2>
    <p>Choose an exercise below to practise in ChatGPT or Claude, or copy the complete prompt into your preferred AI chat.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Review an exercise prompt below, then select <strong>Practise in ChatGPT</strong> or <strong>Practise in Claude</strong> to open it in a new tab.</li>
      <li>If the prompt is still in the message box, press Send. Start voice mode when available and say <strong>“Ready”</strong>. The prompt asks the coach to wait before beginning. For text-only practice, type “Ready” instead.</li>
      <li>If the prompt is missing after sign-in or opening an app, use <strong>Copy prompt</strong> below, paste it into your chat, and send it.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>For spoken practice, see the official <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/features/voice">ChatGPT Voice guide</a> or <a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11101966-use-voice-mode">Claude voice guide</a>. Availability and limits depend on the service, account, and platform. In text-only use, the listening exercise becomes reading and recall practice.</p>
    <p>The buttons pass the public prompt to your chosen service. It may fill the message box or send it automatically, depending on the service and session. The links do not start voice. Your service may show a caution about externally supplied prompts.</p>
    <p>The prompts are free to use. Your AI provider may require an account or paid plan for some features. The link passes the public exercise instructions to your chosen service. This page does not connect to your account or submit your answers.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="exercises-heading">
    <h2 id="exercises-heading">Choose an exercise</h2>
    <p>After “Ready”, share your domain, role, audience, and preferred challenge, or say “use defaults”. For example: “retail shift lead, team briefing, introductory” or “experienced finance analyst, executive audience, challenging”. Ask for plain language, shorter material, or written practice if useful. The coach should supply specialist facts and assess your communication rather than assume ability from your title or experience. These adaptable prompts have not been validated for every domain or role.</p>
    <p><strong>“New example”</strong> changes the scenario. <strong>“Try again”</strong> keeps the facts the same so you can improve your answer. Carry your progress summary into a new chat to help avoid repeating earlier examples; uniqueness across all past sessions is not guaranteed.</p>
    <div class="mt-5 divide-y divide-slate-200">
      {exercises.map((exercise, index) => <details id={exercise.id} class="py-4">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer rounded-lg py-1 font-semibold text-slate-950 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4">{index + 1}. {exercise.name}</summary>
        <p>{exercise.skill}</p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href={practiceUrl('chatgpt', exercise.prompt)} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label={`Practise ${exercise.name} in ChatGPT (opens a new tab)`} class="rounded-lg bg-slate-900 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold !text-white !no-underline focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4">Practise in ChatGPT</a>
          <a href={practiceUrl('claude', exercise.prompt)} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label={`Practise ${exercise.name} in Claude (opens a new tab)`} class="rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold !text-slate-900 !no-underline focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4">Practise in Claude</a>
        </div>
        <label for={`prompt-${exercise.id}`} class="mt-4 block text-sm font-medium text-slate-700">Review the prompt or copy it as a fallback</label>
        <textarea id={`prompt-${exercise.id}`} readonly rows={10} class="mt-2 block w-full resize-y rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-slate-50 p-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-800">{exercise.prompt}</textarea>
        <button type="button" data-copy-prompt={`prompt-${exercise.id}`} class="mt-3 rounded-lg bg-slate-900 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4">Copy prompt</button>
      </details>)}
    </div>
    <p id="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" class="min-h-7 text-sm text-slate-600"></p>
  </section>
  <h2>One way to practise</h2>
  <p>Communication Coach is one option. You can also practise with a trusted colleague or mentor, take a course, join a reading group, or record and review your own explanation. Choose what gives you useful feedback and fits your circumstances; you do not need this tool to begin.</p>
  <p>Five or ten minutes can be a manageable investment in yourself: one exercise, one piece of feedback, one retry. Easy access alone does not make a habit, and competing demands or uncertainty about feedback can make starting difficult. Begin with what works for you and check improvement over time.</p>
  <h2>A ten-minute daily routine</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Spend two minutes reading, listening, or preparing the situation.</li>
    <li>Use three minutes to respond without looking at an answer.</li>
    <li>Review the feedback against the original for two minutes.</li>
    <li>Repeat for three minutes with one deliberate improvement.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Keep your progress</h2>
  <p>At the end, ask: <strong>“Give me a short carry-forward summary with today’s exercise, scenario, one strength, one priority, and the next exercise to try.”</strong> Continue the same conversation or paste that summary into your next one.</p>
  <p>The current coach has no publisher-run database, automatic cross-chat tracking, team dashboard, or built-in reminders. If you want a reminder, set one separately in your calendar or in ChatGPT’s <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/automations">scheduled tasks</a> where supported.</p>
  <h2>What the feedback means</h2>
  <p>Look for an explicit request, accurate recall of constraints, useful clarification, and fewer unsupported assumptions. AI feedback can be mistaken: compare it with your original brief. Ratings are informal coaching judgments, not validated assessments or evidence for hiring and promotion decisions.</p>
  <p>Use fictional or anonymised situations. Your chat is handled by the AI service you choose under its policies. <a href="/communication-coach/privacy">Read the privacy notice</a> and <a href="/communication-coach/terms">terms of use</a>.</p>
  <p>For the research, examples, and management perspective, read <a href={coach.articlePath}>why communication, listening, and comprehension matter in the AI agents era</a>. For help, visit <a href="/communication-coach/support">support</a>.</p>
  <CoachPracticeLinks />
</CoachLayout>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy-prompt]').forEach((button) => {
    button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const field = document.getElementById(button.dataset.copyPrompt ?? '') as HTMLTextAreaElement | null;
      const status = document.getElementById('copy-status');
      if (!field || !status) return;
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(field.value);
        status.textContent = 'Prompt copied. Paste it into your AI chat to begin.';
      } catch {
        field.focus();
        field.select();
        status.textContent = 'Automatic copy is unavailable. The prompt is selected; copy it using your browser or keyboard.';
      }
    });
  });
</script>
